{% extends "quarterly_deep_dive/llm_prompts/base_prompt.j2" %}

{# Specific context for the first callout in Section 9 (Attack Vectors/Complexity) #}
{% set output_format_description = "a brief callout (2-3 sentences) highlighting a single, impactful insight about attack vectors or complexity from the Section 9 data/insights, suitable for a distinct callout box" %}

{% block task_instructions %}
Review the data summaries and chart insights provided below for "{{ section_title }}". This section focuses on the overall distribution of attack vectors and attack complexities across all analyzed CVEs.
Identify the *single most significant finding* from this combined information for administrators. This might be the dominance of a specific attack vector, the prevalence of low-complexity attacks, or a combination of these factors.
Craft a concise callout (2-3 sentences maximum) stating this key finding clearly and its primary implication for defenders.
{% endblock task_instructions %}

